{"session": 1, "turn_no": 1, "world_time": "Sim drill, round 1", "kind": "gm_narration", "summary": "Narration for rt1-1794789940", "actor": "gm", "visibility": "player", "knowledge_type": "fact", "known_to": [], "caused_by": ["evt_0007"], "roll_ids": [], "tags": [], "details": {"text": "The hilt hums in your right hand and the indigo blade snaps alight, washing the sim deck's grid floor in violet. You close the gap in three quick strides, and the near hound's projected hide flickers as it crouches to meet you. Your cut lands clean, a bright seam scored across its flank, and the construct staggers, its outline stuttering where the blade passed. It is hurt, but it is still on its feet, a hand's breadth beyond your blade tip. Behind you, Wick's breathing is loud in the quiet; the far hound paces the right wall, and something behind the crates on your left has gone still. Your action is spent, but your turn is not over: you still have ground to cover if you want it."}, "event_id": "evt_0016", "idempotency_key": "batch:rt1-1794789940:10"}
